This is an interesting idea, but don't underestimate the complexity.

For a (non-computer) RPG I once designed a very small maze like that,
just 4x3 on three levels, that was just a part of a larger dungeon so
it had been deliberately kept small; but it could be observed that it
is not that trivial for the players to handle 3D mazes.

Nonetheless it's a good idea, I think; and a maze significantly larger
than my RPG thing but smaller than your proposal would be interesting.

I am not sure how difficult it would be to implement multiple up/down
stairs consistently and smoothly in Nethack.

About 10 years ago I designed (but never incorporated it in Nethack)
a "chapel" level with a "3D library", inspired by the film "The Name
of the Rose". Meant as a source for spellbooks, but the level full of
fire traps that may, once triggered, chain react and burn the whole
library (or just burn the book atop). The dimensions have also been
deliberately quite conservative small. I copy the 4-level maps part
